<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tony Blair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tony Blair is a British Labour politician who was prime minister of the United Kingdom from 1997 to 2007, the party's longest-serving holder of the office. Leading New Labour to three election victories, he introduced devolution for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, helped secure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> in Northern Ireland, and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> into the wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tony-blair.jpg" alt="Tony Blair" width="320" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pavel Golovkin · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tony_Blair_(2010).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
